{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Working Hard"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Now, What to Do?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to resolve"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to complete "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to tack on a few things that need to be resolved over the week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about work responsibilities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to attend to "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take care of"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That needs attending to first, I think."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fill an order"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to provide what was ordered"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  If the forms aren't files properly, the order won't be filled by the supplier. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "exact"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "accurate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  We need to have an exact idea of what the finished published product will look like."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to finalize"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to complete"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Giving the forms to accounts payable will finalize the order."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to tack on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to add"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd like to tack a couple more things on to the order."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le09ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Need + Verb-ing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you use the verb <span class=\"italic\">need</span>, you talk about what is necessary. You can use a gerund (verb-ing) after the verb <span class=\"italic\">need </span>when you want to  <br/>talk about fixing or improving things, but without saying who is going to do it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + Need + Verb + ing"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The floor <span class=\"strong\">needs washing</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use need with a gerund (v-ing), it has a passive meaning. In other words, the doer or the agent of the sentence is not mentioned because the focus is on the receiver of the action (in the example above, it is the floor)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I know that Mr. Brody already told you what needs doing."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to tack on a few things that need resolving over the week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That needs attending to first, I think."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What exactly needs ordering?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let's go through what needs completing this week."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Clauses with Verb+ing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you use a clause with verb-ing, there are some rules you need to keep in mind."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use a clause with a gerund (verb-ing) as the subject or the complement of a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "As the subject:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Working late at night</span> is stressful.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "As the complement:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">It is stressful <span class=\"strong\">working late at night</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A complement is a group of words that give another word more meaning. You can use them after adjectives, like stressful."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Other clauses with v-ing come after prepositions:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I can get that done quickly <span class=\"strong\">by using my laptop and the mail server</span>. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I can get that done quickly by using my laptop and the mail server. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Most of our inquiries are urgent and require responding promptly. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I can get to the most urgent ones by organizing them by date."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll order the paper using the forms."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Giving the forms to accounts payable will finalize the order."}, {"type": "example", "content": "By filing the forms, you will complete the order."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, make a list of common workplace tasks. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Put them in order for yourself from most enjoyable to least enjoyable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare your list with your partner and explain why your tasks in the order that you did."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you and your partner have different lists, try to trade the tasks that you don't want to do with some of the tasks that your partner doesn't want to do."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of common workplace tasks."}, {"type": "text",